        {
          "id": 3312435878,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "The C/C++ compilers we're most likely to see used are:\n\nGCC, Clang, IBM XL C/C++, Visual Studio C/C++, Intel C/C++, and ~~Sun~~*Oracle* Studio C/C++.\n\nIf I've missed anything, let me know.\n\nIf https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pragma_once#Portability is to be believed:\n\nSufficiently recent versions of those compilers all support `#pragma once`. XL has it as of 13.1.1, and Oracle Studio has it as of 12.5, so those might require more recent versions than, say, GCC, which has had it since 3.4, or Visual Studio, which has had it since 4.2.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
